You can find a list of typical phase names
on page 20 of the PIMBOC guide,

116
00:08:57,370 --> 00:09:04,330
but they could include names such as
build, test transition etc decision points

117
00:09:04,331 --> 00:09:11,670
example funding project go-no-go and
milestone review number three phase gate

118
00:09:11,671 --> 00:09:17,050
this is where you check the project
performance at the end of a phase and

119
00:09:17,051 --> 00:09:22,370
management decides if the projects should
continue you can read more about this on

120
00:09:22,371 --> 00:09:29,150
page 21 of the PIMBOC guide four project
management processes the project life

121
00:09:29,151 --> 00:09:31,747
cycles manage is managed
by executing a series of project

122
00:09:31,748 --> 00:09:35,770
management activities known
as project management processes.

123
00:09:36,730 --> 00:09:42,010
Every project management process produces
one or more outputs from one or more

124
00:09:42,011 --> 00:09:47,570
inputs by using appropriate project
management tools and techniques and you

125
00:09:47,571 --> 00:09:52,190
